  "body": "Reported by the maintainer in chat on 2026-11-16, build v0.22.0 `ef1f5345`; filed by an agent. The maintainer set the priority:\n\n> \"Bug, P1; 2D Adaptive; generate failed: could not generate the toolpath: 2D Adaptive1: invalid machining parameters: setup 'Setup1' holds the part turned (part alignment) - area controls are not supported yet in an aligned setup\"\n\n## What happens\n\n1. Open `testdata/models/fig8.camproj` (model `fig8.step`, vise fixture, stock, tool `EM-0800-4FL`, one 2D Adaptive). The files are in the maintainer's checkout (see #2209).\n2. `Setup1` holds the part turned (part alignment).\n3. The 2D Adaptive has an edge chain selection on the Geometry tab.\n4. Click Generate.\n\nResult: no toolpath. The message is:\n\n```\ngenerate failed: could not generate the toolpath: 2D Adaptive1: invalid machining parameters: setup 'Setup1' holds the part turned (part alignment) - area controls are not supported yet in an aligned setup\n```\n\n## Expected\n\nA 2D Adaptive generates in an aligned setup, with its area selection. A part that is turned onto the vise is a usual setup, and a 2D Adaptive is the usual first roughing operation.\n\n## Facts for the fix\n\n- The refusal is deliberate (\"not supported yet\"). It is not a crash and it does not give a wrong toolpath. The work is to supply the missing behaviour, not to remove the guard.\n- The area controls (the picked chain or face, the boundary) must go through the part alignment transform into the setup frame, with the same transform that the model and the stock use.\n- Find each operation that has the same refusal (search for the message text) and list them on this issue. Fix them with one shared transform, or file one issue for the others.\n- The message does not tell the user what to do. If a case stays refused, the message names the control to clear.\n\n## Safety\n\nThe fix is under the safety floor: it changes where the tool cuts in an aligned setup. A wrong transform (sign, order or pivot) cuts in the wrong place.\n\n- Pin with a setup where the part is turned 90 degrees and the area is not symmetric, so that a wrong frame gives a different region.\n- The verify check and the post gate judge the result against the turned part and the stock.\n- Do not remove the refusal before the transform has its tests.\n\nDone means: `fig8.camproj` generates its 2D Adaptive in the aligned setup; a test pins the cut region against the turned part; each other operation with this refusal is fixed or has its own issue.\n",
